sequenceDiagram
    participant User as Platform User
    participant K8sAPI as Kubernetes API Server<br/>443/TCP HTTPS TLS
    participant Operator as MCP Lifecycle Operator
    participant MCPPod as MCP Server Pod<br/>{port}/TCP HTTP
    participant Prom as Prometheus<br/>8443/TCP HTTPS

    Note over User, MCPPod: Flow 1: MCPServer Reconciliation

    User->>K8sAPI: kubectl apply MCPServer CR
    K8sAPI->>Operator: Watch event (MCPServer created/updated)<br/>HTTPS/TLS, SA Token
    Operator->>K8sAPI: Validate ConfigMap/Secret references<br/>HTTPS/443, SA Token
    K8sAPI-->>Operator: ConfigMap/Secret data

    Operator->>Operator: Compute SHA-256 config hash<br/>of referenced ConfigMaps/Secrets

    Operator->>K8sAPI: Create/Update Deployment<br/>(with config-hash annotation)<br/>HTTPS/443, SA Token
    Operator->>K8sAPI: Create/Update ClusterIP Service<br/>HTTPS/443, SA Token
    Operator->>K8sAPI: Create/Update NetworkPolicy<br/>(ingress-only, MCP port)<br/>HTTPS/443, SA Token

    Note over Operator, MCPPod: MCP Protocol Handshake<br/>(after Deployment Available)

    Operator->>MCPPod: POST initialize (MCP Streamable HTTP)<br/>HTTP/{port}, No Auth
    MCPPod-->>Operator: Server capabilities<br/>(name, version, tools, resources, prompts)

    Operator->>K8sAPI: Update MCPServer status<br/>(serverInfo, conditions)<br/>HTTPS/443, SA Token

    Note over K8sAPI, Operator: Flow 2: ConfigMap/Secret Change Trigger

    K8sAPI->>Operator: Watch event (ConfigMap/Secret changed)<br/>HTTPS/TLS, SA Token
    Operator->>K8sAPI: Lookup MCPServers via field index<br/>HTTPS/443, SA Token
    K8sAPI-->>Operator: Matching MCPServer CRs
    Operator->>Operator: Recompute config hash
    Operator->>K8sAPI: Update Deployment annotation<br/>(triggers rolling update)<br/>HTTPS/443, SA Token

    Note over Prom, Operator: Metrics Collection

    Prom->>Operator: GET /metrics<br/>HTTPS/8443, Bearer Token
    Operator-->>Prom: Prometheus metrics<br/>(reconcile_phase_duration, validation_failures, etc.)
